## Write the distance formula
The distance from $(x_1, y_1)$ to $ax + by + c = 0$ is $\dfrac{|ax_1 + by_1 + c|}{\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}}$.
Here $a = 3$, $b = -4$, $c = -12$ and $(x_1, y_1) = (10, k)$.
## Substitute
d &= \frac{|3(10) - 4(k) - 12|}{\sqrt{3^2 + (-4)^2}}
&= \frac{|30 - 4k - 12|}{\sqrt{9 + 16}}
&= \frac{|18 - 4k|}{\sqrt{25}}
&= \frac{|18 - 4k|}{5}
ANSWER: d = \dfrac{|18 - 4k|}{5}

## Distance from P to l2
Use the same formula with $a = 5$, $b = 12$, $c = -20$.
d_2 &= \frac{|5(10) + 12(k) - 20|}{\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2}}
&= \frac{|30 + 12k|}{\sqrt{169}}
&= \frac{|30 + 12k|}{13}
## Equate the distances
$P$ is on a bisector, so it is the same distance from both lines.
\frac{|18 - 4k|}{5} &= \frac{|30 + 12k|}{13}
13|18 - 4k| &= 5|30 + 12k|
## Case 1: the insides are equal
13(18 - 4k) &= 5(30 + 12k)
234 - 52k &= 150 + 60k
84 &= 112k
k &= \frac{3}{4}
## Case 2: the insides are opposite
13(18 - 4k) &= -5(30 + 12k)
234 - 52k &= -150 - 60k
384 &= -8k
k &= -48
So $k = \frac{3}{4}$ or $k = -48$.
## (ii) Distance from P to l1 when k = 3/4
d &= \frac{|18 - 4k|}{5}
&= \frac{|18 - 3|}{5}
&= \frac{15}{5}
&= 3
ANSWER: k = \dfrac{3}{4} \text{ or } k = -48; \quad d = 3

## Read the centre from the equation
The circle $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2$ has centre $(h,k)$.
Here $h=1$ and $k=-6$ (note $y+6=y-(-6)$), so the centre is $(1,-6)$.
## Find the radius in the form $a\sqrt{10}$
r &= \sqrt{360}
&= \sqrt{36 \times 10}
&= 6\sqrt{10}
ANSWER: \text{Centre } (1,-6), \quad r = 6\sqrt{10}

## Find the ratio in which $K$ divides $[AB]$
Let $A(1,-6)$ be the centre of $s$. Its radius is $3r$ and the radius of $c$ is $r$, where $r=2\sqrt{10}$.
$K$ is $r$ from $B$, so $|KB|=r$ and $|AK|=3r-r=2r$.
So $|AK|:|KB| = 2:1$, and $K$ is the point dividing $[AB]$ in the ratio $2:1$.
## Use the section formula for the $x$-co-ordinate
x_K &= \frac{2(7)+1(1)}{2+1}
&= \frac{15}{3}
&= 5
## Use the section formula for the $y$-co-ordinate
y_K &= \frac{2(12)+1(-6)}{2+1}
&= \frac{18}{3}
&= 6
ANSWER: K = (5, 6)

## Write tan in terms of sin and cos
\tan(A+B) &= \frac{\sin(A+B)}{\cos(A+B)}
## Expand the compound angle formulae
Use $\sin(A+B)=\sin A\cos B+\cos A\sin B$ and $\cos(A+B)=\cos A\cos B-\sin A\sin B$.
&= \frac{\sin A\cos B+\cos A\sin B}{\cos A\cos B-\sin A\sin B}
## Divide top and bottom by $\cos A\cos B$
&= \frac{\dfrac{\sin A\cos B}{\cos A\cos B}+\dfrac{\cos A\sin B}{\cos A\cos B}}{\dfrac{\cos A\cos B}{\cos A\cos B}-\dfrac{\sin A\sin B}{\cos A\cos B}}
## Cancel common factors
&= \frac{\dfrac{\sin A}{\cos A}+\dfrac{\sin B}{\cos B}}{1-\dfrac{\sin A}{\cos A}\cdot\dfrac{\sin B}{\cos B}}
## Replace $\frac{\sin}{\cos}$ by $\tan$
&= \frac{\tan A+\tan B}{1-\tan A\tan B}
ANSWER: \tan(A+B) = \frac{\tan A+\tan B}{1-\tan A\tan B}

## Find the angle in triangle ATB
$\angle HAB$ is the angle at $A$ in the right-angled triangle $ATB$.
\tan|\angle HAB| &= \frac{|BT|}{|AT|} = \frac{160}{60}
&= \frac{8}{3}
|\angle HAB| &= \tan^{-1}\frac{8}{3}
&\approx 69.4439^{\circ}
## Double it, since AB bisects angle HAP
The figure is symmetrical about $AB$.
|\angle HAP| &= 2 \times 69.4439^{\circ}
&\approx 138.9^{\circ}
ANSWER: 138.9^{\circ}

## Write a_{n+1} using p_{n+1}
a_{n+1} &= p - p_{n+1}
&= 0.75 - (0.6 + 0.2\,p_n)
&= 0.75 - 0.6 - 0.2\,p_n
&= 0.15 - 0.2\,p_n
&= 0.2(0.75 - p_n)
&= 0.2\,a_n
## Form the ratio
\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} &= \frac{0.2(0.75 - p_n)}{0.75 - p_n}
&= \frac{1}{5}
The ratio is the same constant for every $n$, so $a_n$ is geometric with common ratio $\frac{1}{5}$.
ANSWER: \frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} = \frac{1}{5}

## Make a right-angled triangle
The two tangent directions are symmetric about the line from Joan to the centre. That line splits $\alpha$ into two equal angles. The tangent point is at a right angle to the radius, so the opposite side is the radius $15$ and the hypotenuse is $150$.
\sin\frac{\alpha}{2} &= \frac{15}{150}
&= 0.1
## Find the half angle and double it
\frac{\alpha}{2} &= \sin^{-1}(0.1)
&\approx 5.7392^{\circ}
\alpha &= 2 \times 5.7392^{\circ}
&\approx 11.5^{\circ}
ANSWER: \alpha = 11.5^{\circ}

## Use the cosine rule in triangle ATH
We know two sides and the angle between them, so use $|AH|^2 = |TA|^2 + |TH|^2 - 2|TA||TH|\cos T$.
|AH|^2 &= 190^2 + 385^2 - 2(190)(385)\cos 18^{\circ}
&= 36100 + 148225 - 146300\cos 18^{\circ}
&= 184325 - 139139.57
&= 45185.43
## Square root
|AH| &= \sqrt{45185.43}
&\approx 212.57
&\approx 213 \text{ m}
ANSWER: |AH| = 213 \text{ m}

## Find when the ball lands (h = 0)
-6t^2 + 22t + 8 &= 0
3t^2 - 11t - 4 &= 0
(3t + 1)(t - 4) &= 0
$t = -\frac{1}{3}$ is rejected because time cannot be negative.
t &= 4
## Find the horizontal distance OB
|OB| &= 38 \times 4
&= 152
## Find the angle of elevation of K from B
In the right-angled triangle $KOB$, $|KO| = 8$ and $|OB| = 152$.
\tan|\angle KBO| &= \frac{8}{152}
&= \frac{1}{19}
|\angle KBO| &= \tan^{-1}\frac{1}{19}
&\approx 3.01^{\circ}
&\approx 3^{\circ}
ANSWER: 3^{\circ}
